  ('saying-what-you-feel', 198, 'Tell a trusted person how you feel about a loved one being far away during a holiday.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 199, 'On a quiet holiday morning, name one feeling before the day fills up.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 200, 'Mark an anniversary of something you got through by telling someone how you feel about it now.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 201, 'Write about how a recent change in your health, home or work makes you feel, using at least three different feeling words.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 202, 'At the turn of a season, list the feelings you had most in the last one and the ones you hope for in the next.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 203, 'Share a feeling about a child growing up, such as pride mixed with a little sadness, with someone who will understand.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 204, 'Tell a parent or caregiver how it feels to see them getting older, if that is a safe and kind conversation for you both.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 205, 'On a long weekend, notice whether rest brings up calm, guilt, boredom or joy. Name which one you feel.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 206, 'Notice your feelings while the rest of the house sleeps. Write one sentence before going to bed.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 207, 'During a spring cleaning or decluttering, notice the feelings that come with letting go of things.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 208, 'Tell a friend how you feel about a season of change at work, such as a reorganization or new boss.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 209, 'Write a few lines about how the first snow, first bloom or first frost makes you feel.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 210, 'Name a feeling about a wedding, baby or celebration in your circle, including any mixed ones.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 211, 'Tell someone how you feel during a holiday when you are working while others are off.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 212, 'Notice your feelings during a commute in the dark. Name them and let them be there.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 213, 'On a warm night, tell someone sitting with you one feeling you are grateful to have today.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 214, 'Share a feeling about the first day in a new place with someone who has been there before.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 215, 'At the very end of a project, when it is finally done, write down how you feel.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 216, 'Notice what feeling comes with the start of a new month and name it before making plans.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 217, 'Tell a friend one feeling you have about the past year as a season or year comes to a close.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 218, 'Once the holidays are over, name one feeling they left behind, such as relief, emptiness or calm.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 219, 'Write how a recent goodbye felt, even a small one like the end of a class or a coworker leaving.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 220, 'When you notice heat in your face during a talk, say "Give me a moment" and take three slow breaths before answering.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 221, 'Write a sentence that links a feeling to a need: "I feel scattered when the mornings are rushed, because I need a slow start."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 222, 'Practice telling someone what you feel without blaming: swap "you made me" for "I felt."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 223, 'Notice a moment today when you felt two opposite things at once. Tell someone about both feelings, not just the easier one.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 224, 'When a friend shares a feeling, say back the feeling you heard: "It sounds like you felt let down."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 225, 'If something you said seemed to land badly, say, "I''m sorry that came out sharp, I was feeling rushed."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 226, 'Answer "How are you?" honestly once today with someone safe: "Honestly, I''m a bit worn down this week."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 227, 'Write one sentence about a feeling and the moment that sparked it: "I felt small during that meeting when my idea was skipped."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 228, 'Try a different shape for a feeling sentence: "What I''m noticing in me right now is" and finish it.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 229, 'When someone shares something hard, ask "What was that like for you?" and let them name the feeling.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 230, 'Say out loud "Part of me feels this, and part of me feels that" about a decision you are weighing.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 231, 'Before reacting to a message that stings, put the phone down and name the feeling in one word.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 232, 'Tell someone, "I need a little time to think about how I feel, can we come back to this tonight?"'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 233, 'Notice how you feel after a difficult talk. Write down whether you said everything you meant to.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 234, 'Say one feeling sentence that ends with what would help: "I''m feeling lonely, and a phone call would really help."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 235, 'When someone thanks you, notice how it feels to receive it. Say "That means a lot to me" if it is true.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 236, 'Ask a friend who seems off, "How are you really doing?" Then listen without rushing to advise.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 237, 'Practice saying a feeling in one breath, short and clear: "I''m frustrated about the plans."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 238, 'Notice when you feel jealous today. Name it privately without scolding yourself for it.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 239, 'Try telling someone how you felt without explaining or justifying it first. Let the feeling stand on its own.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 240, 'Write a feeling sentence about something kind: "I felt warm inside when you saved me a seat."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 241, 'If you snapped at someone, return later and tell them what you were actually feeling underneath.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 242, 'Say "I''m not ready to talk yet, but I will be" when you need space instead of shutting the door completely.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 243, 'Notice whether you wait until a feeling is huge before you say anything. Share one feeling today while it is still small.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 244, 'When someone''s feeling surprises you, say "Thank you for telling me" before saying anything else.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 245, 'Notice a feeling of envy or longing and turn it into a sentence about what you want, then write it down.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 246, 'Share your feelings about a decision someone close to you made, starting with what you understand about it.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 247, 'Write a sentence that names a hard feeling and a soft one at the same time: "I''m angry and I''m also sad."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 248, 'Ask someone, "Did I hurt your feelings earlier?" if you sensed something shift, and be ready to listen.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 249, 'Say "I''m sorry for how that landed" to someone you may have upset, and let them tell you how it felt.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 250, 'Notice what you feel when someone else cries or gets upset. Name your own feeling quietly before you respond.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 251, 'During a disagreement, take a short break by saying "I need a minute to calm down," then come back.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 252, 'Write a feeling sentence that begins with the situation: "When the dishes pile up, I feel discouraged, because I want our home to feel calm."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 253, 'Practice reflecting feelings during a phone call: listen for one feeling word in what the other person says.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 254, 'Notice the feeling under a complaint you have today. Is it worry, hurt or tiredness? Name the true one.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 255, 'Tell someone about a feeling you had that turned out to be wrong, and how it felt to realize that.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 256, 'Try the phrase "I''m noticing I feel" when you want to share something without making it a big deal.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 257, 'When you feel irritated, ask yourself what feeling came just before it. Write both down.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 258, 'Ask someone you trust, "How do you know when I''m upset?" Their answer can teach you about your own signs.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 259, 'Notice the feeling that comes right after you say no to something. Name it, whether it is guilt, relief or pride.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 260, 'Tell someone, "I appreciate you asking, I''m honestly feeling a bit low today," the next time they check in.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 261, 'Let a friend finish describing their feelings before you share a similar story of your own.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 262, 'Write about a time you hid a feeling and what it cost you. Then write what you might say next time.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 263, 'When you feel misunderstood, say "That''s not quite what I meant, can I try again?" and restate your feeling.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 264, 'Notice how you feel after scrolling or watching the news. Name the feeling and tell someone if it lingers.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 265, 'Ask yourself before a hard talk: what do I want them to know about how I feel? Write that one line.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 266, 'Name a feeling about something you are looking forward to, then share it with the person you will do it with.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 267, 'Notice when you feel defensive. Say "I''m feeling a bit defensive, give me a second" out loud.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 268, 'Tell someone you felt grateful for their honesty when they shared a feeling with you.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 269, 'Write two versions of a feeling sentence, one gentle and one blunt. Choose the one that fits the relationship.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 270, 'Notice which feelings you share easily and which you hold back. Pick one held-back feeling to practice voicing.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 271, 'Share a feeling with someone today using only the feeling and the reason, in under fifteen words.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 272, 'When someone shares good news, tell them the feeling it gives you: "I''m so happy for you."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 273, 'Name a feeling while it is happening, instead of afterward: "I''m feeling flustered right now."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 274, 'Notice the moment you start to say "I''m fine" and swap in a truer word, even if it is "tired."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 275, 'Tell someone, "I felt hurt, and I also know you didn''t mean it," if both are true.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 276, 'Opening up often feels easier with people who share their own feelings. Go first today with one small feeling.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 277, 'Write down what you wanted to say in a recent conversation but did not. Practice saying it aloud alone.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 278, 'Tell someone how a gift, gesture or compliment felt to receive, a day or two after the fact.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 279, 'When you feel stuck for words, say, "I''m having trouble finding the words, but it''s something like this."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 280, 'Notice whether a feeling grows or shrinks after you say it out loud. Write what you observe.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 281, 'Ask a partner, friend or family member which feeling they find hardest to say. Share your own answer too.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 282, 'Say a feeling in a softer form first, like "a bit uneasy," and see whether it opens the conversation.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 283, 'Try sharing a feeling using a picture or song with a friend: "This song is exactly how I feel today."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 284, 'After listening to someone''s feelings, ask "Do you want comfort, ideas or just someone to listen?"'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 285, 'Notice how your body relaxes, or does not, after you share a feeling. Write a line about the difference.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 286, 'Write a feeling sentence that names what you hope for: "I feel worried, and I hope we can find a plan together."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 287, 'Practice receiving someone''s hard feeling without defending yourself for one full minute.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 288, 'Name one feeling you tend to cover with humor. Try saying it straight once today.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 289, 'Notice when you feel let down by yourself. Name it kindly, the way you would for a friend.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 290, 'Tell someone who apologized to you how their apology made you feel.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 291, 'Ask someone, "What are you feeling about this?" before sharing your own view on a plan or decision.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 292, 'Name one feeling that surprised you this week, and tell a safe person about it.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 293, 'Look back over this challenge so far and write down which feeling has become easier to say out loud.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 294, 'Choose a color that matches your mood this morning. Tell someone what color you picked and why.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 295, 'Make a small feelings jar: write feelings on slips of paper through the day and read them back tonight.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 296, 'Describe a feeling as weather: sunny, foggy, stormy, breezy. Share your forecast with someone at home.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 297, 'Doodle a quick shape for how you feel right now. Explain the doodle to a friend or keep it in a journal.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 298, 'Pick a photo from your phone that captures how you felt last month. Send it to a friend with one feeling word.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 299, 'Write a six-word story about how you feel today.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 300, 'Read a short poem and underline a line that names something you have felt. Share it with someone.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 301, 'Hum or sing a few bars of a song that fits your mood. Tell someone what mood you were humming.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 302, 'While cooking, name the feeling that comes with the smell of a favorite dish.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 303, 'While folding laundry, let your mind drift and catch the first feeling that surfaces. Name it.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 304, 'During a shower, practice saying a feeling you want to share later in your own words.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 305, 'Write a feeling on a card and tuck it into a book you are reading. Find it again in a week.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 306, 'Notice which feeling words you used most over the past few days. Choose a new word to try this week.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 307, 'Make a short list of phrases that help you start a feelings conversation. Keep it in your wallet or phone notes.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 308, 'Rehearse a feeling conversation in front of a mirror, watching your face as you speak.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 309, 'Ask a friend to practice with you: each of you shares one feeling and the other only says "thank you."'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 310, 'Notice the feeling that comes with finishing a task you had been dreading. Say it out loud.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 311, 'Name one feeling about your body today, such as achy, strong, restless or rested.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 312, 'Notice a feeling during exercise or stretching. Name it between movements.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 313, 'Spend three minutes sitting outside and noticing what feeling nature brings up.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 314, 'Write a feeling with your nondominant hand. Notice whether it comes out more honestly.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 315, 'Name a feeling about money, work or plans in one sentence, then decide who would be safe to share it with.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 316, 'Watching someone else be brave can stir something up. Name it and let it inspire one small share of your own.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 317, 'Tell yourself in the mirror one feeling you are proud you said out loud recently.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 318, 'Write a thank-you note to yourself for a time you named a feeling that was hard to say.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 319, 'Notice which person makes you feel most at ease when sharing. Tell them that, in a sentence.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 320, 'Name a feeling about your home, such as cozy, cramped, peaceful or messy, and share it with someone who lives there.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 321, 'Notice the feeling in your throat before you speak up in a group. Speak anyway, if it feels safe.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 322, 'Write a list of five things that help you calm down enough to name a feeling. Pick one to use today.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 323, 'Listen to a friend talk about their day and name one feeling you heard, gently and without guessing too hard.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 324, 'Name one thing you feel hopeful about in your relationships right now. Share it with someone in them.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 325, 'Write a feeling about a friendship that has drifted. Decide whether you want to reach out, and how.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 326, 'Tell a person in a service job how their kindness made your day feel easier.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 327, 'While waiting for a reply to a message, name the feeling instead of checking your phone again.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 328, 'Picture saying a hard feeling to someone safe, and imagine it going well. Notice how your body responds.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 329, 'Share one small worry with someone who has said they want to hear about your life.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 330, 'Write a feeling sentence in a language or style that feels playful, like a pirate or a sportscaster, to loosen up.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 331, 'Notice how you feel in a crowd compared to alone. Name the difference.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 332, 'Let someone know you feel curious about something they love, and ask them about it.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 333, 'Notice feelings that show up while you eat. Name one before your next bite.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 334, 'Write the feeling you most want to feel this week, and one small thing that could invite it in.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 335, 'Tell someone, "I''ve been practicing saying what I feel, and I want to try with you." Share one feeling.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 336, 'Notice a feeling that fades within a few minutes. Name it as it passes.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 337, 'Name a feeling about a book, movie or show you are enjoying, and tell a friend who would care.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 338, 'Write a note to someone you admire saying how their example makes you feel.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 339, 'Notice the feeling after an honest conversation. Write it down so you remember it next time you hesitate.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 340, 'Pick the one practice from this challenge so far that helped most, and do it again today.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 341, 'Choose a feeling word you have never said aloud before and use it in a real sentence today.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 342, 'Notice your feet on the floor and your back against a chair. Ask what feeling is present underneath the stillness.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 343, 'Share one feeling with a group chat you feel safe in, keeping it light and honest.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 344, 'Tell someone what you feel when you think about your future, using two or three exact words.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 345, 'Notice a feeling that you judge as "bad." Rename it with a word that is honest but kinder.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 346, 'Write a feeling about a pet, a place or a hobby that brings you comfort. Share it with someone who gets it.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 347, 'Ask a friend to tell you one feeling they had today, then offer one of yours in return.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 348, 'Name the feeling you have right after waking from a vivid dream, before it slips away.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 349, 'Notice the feeling you get when someone interrupts you. Name it, and calmly ask to finish your thought.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 350, 'Say "I feel proud of you" to someone today, and tell them exactly what for.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 351, 'Write a feeling sentence for each part of your day: morning, afternoon and evening. Compare them.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 352, 'Notice whether a feeling has a temperature, weight or texture. Describe it in one line.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 353, 'Make a playlist of three songs that match three feelings you had this week. Share one with a friend.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 354, 'Notice your posture when you feel confident. Sit that way while you share a feeling with someone.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 355, 'After a mistake, write the feeling it left you with. Then write one thing you would say to a friend in your place.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 356, 'Tell someone you feel thankful for a lesson they taught you, even if it was long ago.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 357, 'Notice the feeling of being heard after someone listens to you. Name it and thank them.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 358, 'Write down one feeling that you have been carrying for a while, and one safe way you could set it down by sharing it.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 359, 'Ask someone you trust to check in with you this week about a feeling you have shared.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 360, 'Stuck in traffic or a delay? Name the feeling without letting it drive your words.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 361, 'Tell someone what you are looking forward to tomorrow and how it makes you feel.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 362, 'Name a feeling about a goal you are working toward, and share it with someone cheering you on.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 363, 'Look back over this challenge and write a short note about how naming your feelings has changed your conversations.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 364, 'Tell one safe person that you have been working on saying what you feel, and thank them for listening.'),
  ('saying-what-you-feel', 365, 'Finish today by saying one feeling out loud to someone you trust, simply and without apology.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 1, 'Leave five minutes earlier than usual today and notice how the trip feels with a little room in it.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 2, 'Before bed tonight, set your keys, bag and shoes by the door so tomorrow''s departure starts unhurried.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 3, 'When you first sit down in the car or your seat, take one full minute to settle before you do anything else.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 4, 'At the first red light or stop today, loosen your grip on the wheel or the strap and let your hands soften.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 5, 'Let one driver merge in front of you today, and notice whether it costs you anything at all.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 6, 'At a stoplight, keep your eyes on the road and take three slow breaths, longer on the out-breath.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 7, 'Choose what you will listen to before you leave, music, a podcast or quiet, rather than reaching for whatever is on.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 8, 'Look up at the sky once during your trip today and name its color to yourself.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 9, 'Pick one tree along your route and decide to watch how it changes over the coming seasons.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 10, 'Make a small ritual for the moment you start your trip, such as a single deep breath before you turn the key or step out.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 11, 'On the way home, name one task you are leaving at work until tomorrow, and picture setting it on your desk.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 12, 'Hold a door, offer a seat or wave a thank you to one fellow commuter today.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 13, 'If your train or bus runs late today, use the wait to drop your shoulders and look around instead of checking the time again.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 14, 'Take a different street for part of your trip today and notice one thing you have never seen before.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 15, 'If you can, walk one stop or one block farther than usual today and enjoy the extra steps.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 16, 'Ask your carpool partner or rider one question today that has nothing to do with work or school.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 17, 'Riding with kids today? Ask them to point out the first dog, bike or red door they spot.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 18, 'Working from home? Take a ten minute walk around the block before you open your laptop, as your own small commute.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 19, 'At each stop today, check your jaw and let your teeth part slightly.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 20, 'Pack tomorrow''s lunch or snack tonight so the morning has one less thing to rush.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 21, 'Fill your gas tank or charge your transit card this evening, before it becomes a morning scramble.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 22, 'Notice the first building you pass that you find beautiful, and give it a second look when it is safe.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 23, 'On a rainy day, leave a few extra minutes and let the sound of the rain be your soundtrack for part of the trip.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 24, 'When you park or get off today, sit or stand still for ten seconds before heading in.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 25, 'Smile at one bus driver, crossing guard or parking attendant today.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 26, 'Set your car seat, mirrors and temperature before you pull out, so you are comfortable from the start.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 27, 'If someone cuts you off today, say "they must be in a hurry" out loud and let the moment pass.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 28, 'Plan your route the night before so you are not deciding while you drive.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 29, 'Ride in silence for the first five minutes of your trip and listen to what is around you.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 30, 'At a red light, roll your shoulders back twice while keeping your eyes on the road ahead.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 31, 'Lay out tomorrow''s clothes tonight, including a layer for the weather.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 32, 'Count how many shades of green you can see from the bus or train window today.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 33, 'Choose one song that calms you and save it for the hardest stretch of your trip.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 34, 'Step off the train or bus and pause for one breath on the platform before walking on.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 35, 'Leave your cell phone in your bag for the first part of your ride and look out the window instead.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 36, 'Notice one sign of the current season on your route, a fallen leaf, a bud, a puddle or a patch of frost.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 37, 'As you pull into your driveway or reach your front door, say one word that describes how you want your evening to feel.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 38, 'Give a pedestrian or cyclist extra space and time at a crosswalk today.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 39, 'When traffic stops entirely, rest your hands at the bottom of the wheel and unclench your fingers one at a time.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 40, 'Bike or walk part of your route today if the weather and distance allow.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 41, 'Notice the temperature of the air the moment you step outside this morning.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 42, 'Tonight, check the weather for tomorrow so you are not surprised by rain or cold at the door.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 43, 'Pick a podcast or audiobook episode tonight so tomorrow''s trip begins with something you chose.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 44, 'Wave a thank you to the next driver who lets you in.'),
  ('a-gentler-commute', 45, 'As you wait at a crosswalk, feel your weight shift evenly between both feet.'),
